  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ensure respect for, promote and realize fundamental principles and rights at work</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malawi launched its second National Action Plan on Child Labour (NAP-II, 2020 &#x2013; 2025) on 12 June 2020. The Government of Malawi adopted the NAP II and operationalize it in consultation with social partners, a comprehensive and gender-responsive strategy or action plan to tackle child labour. This has facilitated resource allocation for its implementation and identified specific measures aimed at the elimination of child labour included in the action plan are implemented. ILO participated in the discussions and meeting in the drafting of the Malawi&apos;s second National Action Plan on Child Labour (NAP-II, 2020 &#x2013; 2025), launched by the Minister of Labour on 12 June 2020 as part of national commemorations of World Day Against Child Labour (WDACL). ILO input was incorporated into the final NAP II document.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">7.1.3. Number of member States with newly adopted or updated strategies and action plans to tackle child labour in all its forms</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
